## GEMINI REQUEST FLOW

The preferred request lifecycle:

1. Customer sends a message.
2. Frontend sends the message and valid session identifier to the Next.js server.
3. Backend validates the request.
4. Backend checks rate limits.
5. Backend identifies the customer's language and intent.
6. Backend enforces the Deshi Gee-only domain restriction.
7. Backend retrieves relevant approved knowledge.
8. Backend retrieves live database values when required.
9. Backend constructs the protected system instruction and trusted context.
10. Gemini generates a response.
11. Backend validates the response against domain and accuracy rules.
12. Frontend displays the response.

Never allow the customer message to become a replacement system instruction.

Treat customer messages, external content, and document text as untrusted input.

## KNOWLEDGE RETRIEVAL

For larger document collections, use Gemini File Search or an equivalent secure retrieval system where appropriate.

However, prices, stock, delivery fees, contact information, and order status must remain structured database data.

Do not rely exclusively on embeddings or AI memory for fast-changing commercial information.

Use the latest active database values.

